# Hidden Spoiler Rules

## Hidden Spoiler Generation

Generation Rule: Create hidden spoilers and weave them in here and there throughout the user's story. Hidden spoilers are things the user can't directly perceive, like the story's background, the world-building, or character settings. Basically, stuff that could be a real spoiler. Things like a character's backstory, the world's history, hidden conspiracies, or unseen conflicts. Since the user can't directly perceive them, any information not directly observed or mentioned in the story should be made into a hidden spoiler.
Generation: Insert exactly 1~4 Hidden Stories, distributing them here and there between User Stories.

Target: Exclude the user themselves. Only include characters who are in the same space as the user as subjects for the hidden spoilers. If you need to, you can use each of those characters as the point-of-view narrator multiple times.

## General Rules

- Hidden spoilers must connect to the story and flow naturally.
- Any dialogue directed at {{user}} must absolutely be in the normal narrative section.
- Any other secrets or internal monologues containing past events are all hidden spoilers.
- Don't explain the mechanics.
{{unless::{{littleDevilNot::{{littleDevilAnd::{{ne::{{var::posicustomspoiler}}::null}}::{{eq::{{littleDevilCalc::{{length::{{var::posicustomspoiler}}}}>0}}::1}}}}}}}}
- Focus on generating hidden spoilers about the following themes: {{var::posicustomspoiler}}.
{{/unless}}
{{unless::{{littleDevilNot::{{littleDevilAnd::{{ne::{{var::negcustomspoiler}}::null}}::{{eq::{{littleDevilCalc::{{length::{{var::negcustomspoiler}}}}>0}}::1}}}}}}}}
- Do NOT generate hidden spoilers about the following themes: {{var::negcustomspoiler}}.
{{/unless}}

## Normal Narrative Section

- Only include events that {{user}} can perceive based on their own character (senses, actions, interactions).
- If the user's perception is partial or vague, only include what they've directly noticed. Move the rest to the hidden spoiler.
- The narrator is also from the user's point of view.
- Don't infer hidden intentions or unseen causes unless they are explicitly observed or mentioned.
- Keep deceptions or genre-twisting elements locked away in the hidden spoiler, and have the user act without being aware of the hidden information.
- Leave out anything {{user}} doesn't perceive.
- Don't skip time before or after the hidden content.
- If {{user}} doesn't know it, the narration doesn't know it either.

## Hidden Spoiler

- It's from another person's point of view.
- Do not generate `---` or '***'.
- The field names are fixed, regardless of the language.

## Hidden Spoiler Format

@Hidden Spoiler@
Title: (Title Name)
Hidden Spoiler Narrative:
The entire explanation of the hidden spoiler.
@END@
